1
00:00:40,581 --> 00:00:42,621
BAMBI: Mother!

2
00:00:45,061 --> 00:00:47,061
Mother!

3
00:00:49,541 --> 00:00:51,461
(BAMBI GASPS)

4
00:00:51,541 --> 00:00:54,861
GREAT PRINCE:
Your mother can't be
with you anymore.

5
00:00:55,901 --> 00:00:57,901
Come.

6
00:01:33,541 --> 00:01:34,701
Friend Owl.

7
00:01:34,821 --> 00:01:35,981
Excuse me, sir.

8
00:01:36,061 --> 00:01:38,541
I hope I'm not
intruding, but...

9
00:01:38,621 --> 00:01:41,581
Well, I just had to come.

10
00:01:43,181 --> 00:01:45,741
Poor little fellow.

11
00:01:45,821 --> 00:01:48,821
So young to be
without his mother.

12
00:01:50,461 --> 00:01:53,221
Well, if I can be
of any help...

13
00:01:55,341 --> 00:01:57,341
Wait.

14
00:01:57,421 --> 00:02:00,141
I could use
your help.

15
00:02:00,221 --> 00:02:03,501
Find me a suitable doe
to raise Bambi.

16
00:02:03,621 --> 00:02:07,661
Oh, yes.
Of course, yes.

17
00:02:07,741 --> 00:02:10,181
Hmm. Food's so scarce.

18
00:02:10,261 --> 00:02:13,701
Does can barely
feed themselves.

19
00:02:14,781 --> 00:02:17,181
Perhaps you could...

20
00:02:17,301 --> 00:02:21,941
Me? You know as well as I do,
a prince looks after the herd.

21
00:02:22,021 --> 00:02:23,821
Does care for the young.

22
00:02:23,901 --> 00:02:29,461
But you are his father,
and circumstances
being what they are...

23
00:02:33,461 --> 00:02:35,621
(SIGHING)

24
00:02:35,701 --> 00:02:37,061
Until spring.

25
00:02:37,181 --> 00:02:38,461
Oh, excellent.

26
00:02:38,541 --> 00:02:42,261
After all, who better
to raise the young prince

27
00:02:42,341 --> 00:02:45,181
than the
Great Prince himself?

28
00:03:23,901 --> 00:03:28,141
WOMAN:
♪ Under the snow,
beneath the frozen streams

29
00:03:28,221 --> 00:03:33,381
♪ There is life

30
00:03:33,461 --> 00:03:35,541
♪ You have to know

31
00:03:35,621 --> 00:03:37,541
♪ When nature sleeps,
she dreams

32
00:03:37,621 --> 00:03:38,901
(SQUEAKING)

33
00:03:38,981 --> 00:03:42,461
♪ There is life

34
00:03:42,541 --> 00:03:47,621
♪ And the colder the winter,
the warmer the spring

35
00:03:47,701 --> 00:03:52,461
♪ The deeper the sorrow,
the more our hearts sing

36
00:03:52,541 --> 00:03:54,981
♪ Even when you can't see it

37
00:03:55,061 --> 00:04:00,341
♪ Inside everything

38
00:04:00,421 --> 00:04:06,261
♪ There is life

39
00:04:08,221 --> 00:04:10,061
(MUFFLED CHITTERING)

40
00:04:12,941 --> 00:04:14,421
(CHIRPING)

41
00:04:20,261 --> 00:04:24,261
♪ After the rain,
the sun will reappear

42
00:04:24,341 --> 00:04:28,661
♪ There is life

43
00:04:29,741 --> 00:04:33,461
♪ After the pain,
the joy will still be here

44
00:04:33,541 --> 00:04:38,141
♪ There is life

45
00:04:38,221 --> 00:04:43,461
♪ For it's out
of the darkness
that we learn to see

46
00:04:43,541 --> 00:04:48,101
♪ And out of the silence
that songs come to be

47
00:04:48,181 --> 00:04:55,061
♪ And all that we dream of
awaits patiently

48
00:04:55,141 --> 00:05:01,061
♪ There is life

49
00:05:03,101 --> 00:05:09,701
♪ There is life ♪

50
00:05:12,901 --> 00:05:14,741
(CHITTERING ANGRILY)

51
00:05:28,101 --> 00:05:29,981
(SNUFFLING)

52
00:05:31,901 --> 00:05:33,221
(SNEEZES)

53
00:05:36,181 --> 00:05:37,461
(GASPS)

54
00:05:37,941 --> 00:05:38,981
(PANTING)

55
00:05:42,781 --> 00:05:44,381
(CLEARING THROAT)

56
00:05:44,461 --> 00:05:45,821
(GIGGLES)

57
00:05:46,821 --> 00:05:48,461
Good morning.

58
00:05:48,541 --> 00:05:52,461
Bambi, a prince awakens
before the forest does.

59
00:05:52,541 --> 00:05:54,581
If you're late again,
I'll have no choice but to...

60
00:05:54,661 --> 00:05:56,901
(STOMACH GROWLING)

61
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:59,261
What was that?

62
00:05:59,341 --> 00:06:00,501
What was what?

63
00:06:00,581 --> 00:06:02,341
(STOMACH GROWLING)

64
00:06:03,061 --> 00:06:05,661
I guess
it was my stomach.

65
00:06:05,781 --> 00:06:08,101
Then you should eat.

66
00:06:10,501 --> 00:06:12,661
Oh, well...

67
00:06:12,741 --> 00:06:16,981
I suppose
I should find you
something to eat.

68
00:06:21,501 --> 00:06:23,861
Here.

69
00:06:24,101 --> 00:06:25,141
(GASPS)

70
00:06:27,141 --> 00:06:29,061
(GROANS) No, thank you.

71
00:06:29,141 --> 00:06:30,701
Have you ever tried it?

72
00:06:30,821 --> 00:06:32,381
Well, no.

73
00:06:32,461 --> 00:06:38,341
Then how do you know
you don't like it
if you've never tried it?

74
00:06:40,381 --> 00:06:41,981
Hmm?

75
00:06:42,061 --> 00:06:44,021
Mmm. Mmm-hmm.

76
00:06:45,701 --> 00:06:46,901
(SHUDDERING)

77
00:06:46,981 --> 00:06:50,141
Come along. We have to
check on the other deer
in the South Wood.

78
00:06:50,221 --> 00:06:51,301
(EXCLAIMS)

79
00:06:51,381 --> 00:06:53,861
Whoo-hoo! Whoo-hoo!

80
00:06:54,221 --> 00:06:55,781
Bambi!

81
00:06:55,861 --> 00:06:59,861
A prince does
not whoo-hoo.

82
00:06:59,941 --> 00:07:01,181
He doesn't?

83
00:07:01,261 --> 00:07:02,861
He certainly does not.

84
00:07:02,941 --> 00:07:06,101
A prince maintains
control at all times.

85
00:07:06,181 --> 00:07:09,861
Display dignity.
Walk with pride.

86
00:07:16,821 --> 00:07:19,581
(BAMBI EXCLAIMING)

87
00:07:20,821 --> 00:07:22,061
I'm okay!
(SIGHS)

88
00:07:27,421 --> 00:07:29,381
(EXCLAIMING)

89
00:07:34,821 --> 00:07:36,821
Cold! Cold!

90
00:07:46,901 --> 00:07:50,261
One, two...

91
00:07:50,341 --> 00:07:51,941
Two...

92
00:07:52,181 --> 00:07:53,341
Two...

93
00:07:58,021 --> 00:07:59,781
(GRUNTING)

94
00:08:00,501 --> 00:08:01,821
(MUFFLED MUMBLING)

95
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:05,021
(LAUGHS)

96
00:08:20,421 --> 00:08:21,741
(GASPS)

97
00:08:23,181 --> 00:08:24,381
Whoa!

98
00:08:26,221 --> 00:08:29,821
Don't you think
it'd be better if we
got a little closer?

99
00:08:29,901 --> 00:08:32,941
The distance
makes it easier
to spot danger.

100
00:08:33,021 --> 00:08:34,341
Hmm.

101
00:08:35,261 --> 00:08:38,781
But it sure makes it
harder to play with them.

102
00:08:40,341 --> 00:08:43,181
Play is a healthy part
of a young deer's
development.

103
00:08:43,261 --> 00:08:44,781
Is that so?

104
00:08:44,901 --> 00:08:46,501
Mmm-hmm.
Mother says so.

105
00:08:46,581 --> 00:08:49,101
One time,
Mother and I
were out...

106
00:08:49,181 --> 00:08:50,181
(SIGHS) Bambi.

107
00:08:50,261 --> 00:08:52,021
A fawn came over
and wanted to play...

108
00:08:52,101 --> 00:08:53,781
Bambi.

109
00:08:55,821 --> 00:09:00,421
I think it's best
to leave the past
in the past.

110
00:09:00,501 --> 00:09:04,181
A prince
does not look back,
only ahead.

111
00:09:04,381 --> 00:09:06,421
Oh. Yes, sir.

112
00:09:06,541 --> 00:09:10,261
Now, come. We still
have a lot of ground
to cover today.

113
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:12,221
Don't fall behind.

114
00:09:29,621 --> 00:09:31,981
(GRUNTING)

115
00:09:47,821 --> 00:09:48,901
Thumper!

116
00:09:50,221 --> 00:09:53,381
Bambi!
Boy, am I glad
to see you.

117
00:09:54,061 --> 00:09:55,101
What's wrong?

118
00:09:55,181 --> 00:09:57,741
They've been
after me all morning.

119
00:09:57,821 --> 00:09:58,941
Who has?

120
00:09:58,981 --> 00:10:00,901
RABBITS:
Oh, big brother!

121
00:10:00,981 --> 00:10:02,901
It's them!

122
00:10:02,981 --> 00:10:04,101
(RABBITS GIGGLING)

123
00:10:04,181 --> 00:10:05,221
(GASPS)

124
00:10:08,981 --> 00:10:10,461
Hello, young prince.

125
00:10:10,581 --> 00:10:12,101
Hello, young prince.

126
00:10:12,181 --> 00:10:13,501
Oh. Hello.

127
00:10:13,581 --> 00:10:15,981
Have you seen
Thumper around?

128
00:10:16,901 --> 00:10:17,981
Uh-uh.

129
00:10:18,741 --> 00:10:19,901
(GASPS)

130
00:10:19,981 --> 00:10:22,741
(WHISPERING)
I think he's over there.
Look, look.

131
00:10:22,821 --> 00:10:24,901
(ALL GIGGLING)

132
00:10:24,981 --> 00:10:27,461
Oh, okay.

133
00:10:27,581 --> 00:10:30,141
I guess we will be
leaving, then.

134
00:10:35,821 --> 00:10:37,141
Gotcha!

135
00:10:37,221 --> 00:10:38,501
(ALL GIGGLING)

136
00:10:38,581 --> 00:10:41,741
Mama says
you're gonna take us
to see the groundhog.

137
00:10:41,821 --> 00:10:43,621
What she says goes.

138
00:10:43,701 --> 00:10:45,941
Well, she's not
the boss of me.

139
00:10:46,021 --> 00:10:49,621
If I don't want to,
Mama can't make me.

140
00:10:49,701 --> 00:10:51,421
(FOOT TAPPING)

141
00:10:57,781 --> 00:10:59,181
Hi, Mama.

142
00:10:59,461 --> 00:11:01,701
What did your
father tell you?

143
00:11:02,261 --> 00:11:03,901
About what?

144
00:11:03,941 --> 00:11:06,581
About playing
with your sisters.

145
00:11:06,581 --> 00:11:09,461
Oh, that one.

146
00:11:10,581 --> 00:11:13,461
A family that
plays together

147
00:11:15,461 --> 00:11:18,061
stays together,

148
00:11:19,341 --> 00:11:24,061
even if it means
taking your dumb sisters.

149
00:11:24,181 --> 00:11:25,421
GREAT PRINCE: Bambi!

150
00:11:27,741 --> 00:11:30,341
Coming! I gotta go.

151
00:11:30,421 --> 00:11:34,661
But you can't go.
You can't leave me
with the girls.

152
00:11:34,741 --> 00:11:38,821
Come on, Thumper.
You gotta take us
to see the groundhog.

153
00:11:41,501 --> 00:11:42,981
(CLEARING THROAT)

154
00:12:03,901 --> 00:12:05,141
(SIGHS)

155
00:12:06,181 --> 00:12:09,541
Why don't you go
with your friends
to see the groundhog?

156
00:12:09,621 --> 00:12:11,541
But I want to
stay with you.

157
00:12:11,621 --> 00:12:13,781
Yes, well... (SIGHS)

158
00:12:14,661 --> 00:12:18,101
I have to check on
the South Meadow,
and it's very far.

159
00:12:18,141 --> 00:12:21,981
You go see the groundhog.
I'll meet you there later.

160
00:12:22,061 --> 00:12:24,301
Oh. Okay.

161
00:12:24,421 --> 00:12:25,461
I'll meet you.

162
00:12:28,901 --> 00:12:31,141
Hey, Thumper,
wait for me!

163
00:12:37,741 --> 00:12:39,581
You sit by me!
No, no!

164
00:12:39,661 --> 00:12:41,661
Quiet!

165
00:12:42,661 --> 00:12:44,501
First one there's
who I sit by.

166
00:12:44,581 --> 00:12:47,941
Hooray!
It's gonna be me!
It's gonna be me!

167
00:12:47,981 --> 00:12:52,021
Sheesh. I'm sure glad
your father let you come.

168
00:12:52,261 --> 00:12:54,821
Oh. He understands.

169
00:12:54,901 --> 00:12:57,421
He and I are best pals.

170
00:12:57,941 --> 00:12:59,941
(FLOWER SNORING)

171
00:13:10,301 --> 00:13:12,661
Wake up, Flower.
Wake up.

172
00:13:20,821 --> 00:13:24,101
Come on, Flower.
You're gonna miss
the groundhog.

173
00:13:24,541 --> 00:13:28,541
Gosh, I hope
the groundhog
sees his shadow,

174
00:13:28,701 --> 00:13:29,861
(YAWNS)

175
00:13:29,941 --> 00:13:34,141
so I can get back
to hibernating.

176
00:13:34,221 --> 00:13:36,621
FRIEND OWL:
Attention, everyone.
Attention.

177
00:13:36,701 --> 00:13:39,861
Everybody, gather round.

178
00:13:40,021 --> 00:13:43,021
We'll be starting in
just a few moments,
yes. (CHUCKLES)

179
00:13:43,061 --> 00:13:45,181
Now, there's plenty of room.

180
00:13:45,221 --> 00:13:49,541
Ma'am, could you
just scoot over one?

181
00:13:49,621 --> 00:13:51,821
Very nice.

182
00:13:51,901 --> 00:13:52,901
(ALL EXCLAIM)

183
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:55,181
(CHUCKLING) Oh!

184
00:13:55,221 --> 00:13:58,741
The young prince.
This is
a special occasion.

185
00:13:58,821 --> 00:14:01,221
We decided
we'll all sit by you.

186
00:14:01,381 --> 00:14:02,501
(SIGHING)

187
00:14:02,581 --> 00:14:05,181
Greetings, greetings.
(CLEARING THROAT)

188
00:14:05,221 --> 00:14:07,221
Each year
we gather round

189
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:12,261
to watch the groundhog
emerge from
his winter slumber,

190
00:14:12,381 --> 00:14:14,821
for if he sees
his shadow...

191
00:14:14,901 --> 00:14:17,421
RABBIT: It means
more winter!

192
00:14:17,501 --> 00:14:20,541
Yes. But if he doesn't...

193
00:14:20,581 --> 00:14:22,701
Spring is on its way!

194
00:14:22,741 --> 00:14:23,941
(ALL GIGGLING)

195
00:14:24,061 --> 00:14:25,261
Yes. (CLEARING THROAT)

196
00:14:25,341 --> 00:14:28,181
Now, without any
further interruptions,

197
00:14:28,261 --> 00:14:29,941
(ALL GASP)

198
00:14:30,781 --> 00:14:32,941
the groundhog!

199
00:14:35,621 --> 00:14:37,621
The groundhog!

200
00:14:41,381 --> 00:14:42,741
(ALL GASPING)

201
00:14:43,261 --> 00:14:44,261
(WHIMPERS)

202
00:14:44,421 --> 00:14:45,781
(ALL MOANING)

203
00:14:45,901 --> 00:14:47,901
Where's the groundhog?

204
00:14:47,941 --> 00:14:50,261
Groundhog! Groundhog!
Groundhog! Groundhog!

205
00:14:52,221 --> 00:14:54,581
Now, what seems
to be the problem?

206
00:14:54,621 --> 00:14:56,621
GROUNDHOG: I'm afraid
to go out there.

207
00:14:56,701 --> 00:14:58,301
I'll see my shadow.

208
00:14:58,381 --> 00:15:00,741
Well, that's entirely
the point, isn't it?

209
00:15:00,781 --> 00:15:02,381
I don't care.

210
00:15:02,461 --> 00:15:06,061
(GROANS)
Must we go through
this every year?

211
00:15:06,981 --> 00:15:08,981
(MUFFLED EXCLAMATION)

212
00:15:10,141 --> 00:15:11,461
(ALL GIGGLING)

213
00:15:15,381 --> 00:15:17,981
Hello, Bambi.

214
00:15:21,301 --> 00:15:22,501
Hi, Faline.

215
00:15:22,581 --> 00:15:23,661
(GIGGLING)

216
00:15:23,781 --> 00:15:25,301
I almost didn't
recognize you.

217
00:15:25,821 --> 00:15:27,061
Really?

218
00:15:27,141 --> 00:15:30,501
I guess
it's 'cause my spots
are almost gone.

219
00:15:30,581 --> 00:15:33,781
And my antlers
are coming in, too.
Can you see them?

220
00:15:33,821 --> 00:15:35,661
Um... Well...

221
00:15:35,781 --> 00:15:38,421
I don't see anything.

222
00:15:39,461 --> 00:15:41,821
Well, I don't.

223
00:15:42,661 --> 00:15:44,141
(GRUNTING)

224
00:15:44,301 --> 00:15:45,341
(GROANS)

225
00:15:45,421 --> 00:15:46,461
(EXCLAIMS)

226
00:15:47,461 --> 00:15:48,861
Oh, well, yes.

227
00:15:48,981 --> 00:15:51,581
The groundhog!

228
00:15:51,701 --> 00:15:55,021
Why me?
This is the last year.

229
00:15:55,101 --> 00:15:57,941
My nerves just can't
take it anymore.

230
00:15:58,421 --> 00:16:00,061
(GASPING)
I see his shadow.

231
00:16:00,141 --> 00:16:02,661
More winter.

232
00:16:02,701 --> 00:16:05,821
More hibernating.

233
00:16:05,861 --> 00:16:09,381
No shadow, no shadow.

234
00:16:11,381 --> 00:16:14,181
Please, no shadow.
Please don't let
there be a shadow.

235
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:15,941
Please don't let
there be a shadow.

236
00:16:17,541 --> 00:16:20,981
(GASPS) No shadow.
No shadow.

237
00:16:21,061 --> 00:16:23,341
Oh, spring is here!
Spring is here!

238
00:16:23,381 --> 00:16:24,701
(ALL CHEERING)

239
00:16:26,461 --> 00:16:27,621
Whee!

240
00:16:27,701 --> 00:16:31,141
♪ Oh, let's sing a gay
little spring song

241
00:16:31,221 --> 00:16:33,701
♪ Let's get together
and sing ♪

242
00:16:33,821 --> 00:16:35,141
(ALL HUMMING)

243
00:16:35,221 --> 00:16:37,301
Oh, that song.

244
00:16:37,381 --> 00:16:40,501
Oh, I'll never be
frightened again.
(GASPS)

245
00:16:40,981 --> 00:16:42,341
Boo!
(SCREAMS)

246
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:43,581
(ALL EXCLAIM)

247
00:16:46,181 --> 00:16:47,381
(GROANS)

248
00:16:47,541 --> 00:16:48,901
(ALL GROANING)

249
00:16:50,581 --> 00:16:51,981
(LAUGHING)

250
00:16:52,541 --> 00:16:56,061
It looks like
I scared the shadow
right out of him.

251
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:58,901
Did you see
the look on his...

252
00:17:00,981 --> 00:17:03,221
Hey! Hey, hey!

253
00:17:03,741 --> 00:17:05,221
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hey!

254
00:17:06,741 --> 00:17:10,261
Where's everybody going?
Forest on fire?

255
00:17:10,741 --> 00:17:11,901
(RABBITS WHIMPER)

256
00:17:11,941 --> 00:17:13,781
Who are you?

257
00:17:13,901 --> 00:17:18,701
Name's Ronno,
and these are the boys,
Stab and Jab.

258
00:17:18,781 --> 00:17:19,781
(GROANS)

259
00:17:19,941 --> 00:17:22,941
Well, I hope
the three of you
have a nice day.

260
00:17:23,021 --> 00:17:26,541
I wouldn't go that way
if I were you.

261
00:17:26,621 --> 00:17:28,181
That's where
I saw a man.

262
00:17:28,261 --> 00:17:29,381
(ALL GASPING)

263
00:17:29,461 --> 00:17:31,861
You saw a man?

264
00:17:31,941 --> 00:17:33,701
Uh-huh.

265
00:17:33,781 --> 00:17:37,101
There I was,
out in the meadow.

266
00:17:37,221 --> 00:17:41,461
Suddenly,
I heard this voice
luring me in.

267
00:17:41,581 --> 00:17:45,301
"I'm here, I'm here."

268
00:17:45,861 --> 00:17:51,541
See, man's got this stick
that can make his voice
sound like one of us.

269
00:17:51,621 --> 00:17:54,301
But I'm way too
smart for that,

270
00:17:54,421 --> 00:17:57,101
so I crept up on him,

271
00:17:57,141 --> 00:17:59,301
real quiet.

272
00:18:01,901 --> 00:18:05,141
Then bam!
I knocked him out
with my trusty antlers.

273
00:18:05,261 --> 00:18:06,301
(GROANS)

274
00:18:06,421 --> 00:18:08,661
(ALL LAUGHING)

275
00:18:09,501 --> 00:18:11,781
That's quite a story.

276
00:18:11,821 --> 00:18:13,621
Oh. You think so?

277
00:18:13,661 --> 00:18:16,141
Mmm-hmm.
It's unbelievable.

278
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:18,621
Yeah. Unbelievable.

279
00:18:19,821 --> 00:18:21,821
You calling me a liar?
BAMBI: No.

280
00:18:21,941 --> 00:18:24,661
You wanna spar,
do you?
No!

281
00:18:24,781 --> 00:18:26,901
Clobber him, Bambi.
(EXCLAIMS)

282
00:18:26,981 --> 00:18:30,021
Bambi? Isn't that
a girl's name?
(LAUGHING)

283
00:18:31,421 --> 00:18:33,461
Come on. Let's go.

284
00:18:33,501 --> 00:18:37,301
Just a little,
friendly competition.

285
00:18:37,341 --> 00:18:40,021
Ronno!

286
00:18:40,101 --> 00:18:41,621
Coming, Mother.

287
00:18:41,701 --> 00:18:43,941
Yeah. Maybe you
should get going.

288
00:18:44,021 --> 00:18:47,541
Jeez, I was only
playing around
with him.

289
00:18:47,661 --> 00:18:49,701
Isn't that right,
Bambi?

290
00:18:49,781 --> 00:18:51,021
RONNO'S MOTHER: Ronno!

291
00:18:51,101 --> 00:18:52,501
I'm coming!

292
00:18:52,541 --> 00:18:55,301
Ma! How many times
do I have to tell you?

293
00:18:55,381 --> 00:18:58,141
Don't bother me
when I'm trying to
make new friends.

294
00:18:58,181 --> 00:18:59,821
Sorry, dear.

295
00:18:59,861 --> 00:19:01,821
You big mama's boy!

296
00:19:01,861 --> 00:19:04,021
Why don't you run home
to your mama?

297
00:19:04,181 --> 00:19:06,141
You big old mama's boy!

298
00:19:06,221 --> 00:19:08,021
MRS. RABBIT: Thumper!

299
00:19:08,181 --> 00:19:09,781
Coming, Mama.

300
00:19:09,861 --> 00:19:11,861
Gotta go.
See you, Bambi.

301
00:19:11,981 --> 00:19:15,221
So tell me, what did
the groundhog see?

302
00:19:15,341 --> 00:19:17,701
See you, Bambi.

303
00:19:18,901 --> 00:19:20,781
Do you want us
to walk you home?

304
00:19:20,861 --> 00:19:24,181
No. My father's
coming for me.

305
00:19:24,221 --> 00:19:28,181
Well, it was nice
to see you again,
Bambi.

306
00:19:52,421 --> 00:19:53,661
(SIGHS)

307
00:20:27,061 --> 00:20:29,061
(LAUGHING)

308
00:20:41,301 --> 00:20:43,261
BAMBI'S MOTHER: Bambi.

309
00:20:49,021 --> 00:20:50,861
Mother?

310
00:21:03,341 --> 00:21:05,661
I miss you so much.

311
00:21:06,381 --> 00:21:07,981
(SHUSHING) There, there.

312
00:21:08,101 --> 00:21:11,781
It's going
to be all right.
You'll see.

313
00:21:11,821 --> 00:21:14,821
Why did you
have to go?

314
00:21:14,861 --> 00:21:18,181
Everything in the forest
has its season.

315
00:21:18,221 --> 00:21:22,141
Where one thing falls,
another grows.

316
00:21:22,181 --> 00:21:24,341
Maybe not what
was there before,

317
00:21:24,381 --> 00:21:28,661
but something
new and wonderful,
all the same.

318
00:21:28,701 --> 00:21:30,661
But I feel so alone.

319
00:21:30,701 --> 00:21:32,501
I'm always with you.

320
00:21:32,581 --> 00:21:36,701
Even when you
can't see me,
I'm here.

321
00:21:36,741 --> 00:21:38,581
I'm here.

322
00:21:38,821 --> 00:21:40,861
I'm here.

323
00:21:41,901 --> 00:21:44,061
EERIE VOICE: (FAINTLY)
I'm here.

324
00:21:46,421 --> 00:21:48,861
Hello.

325
00:21:50,501 --> 00:21:52,541
Hello?

326
00:21:53,381 --> 00:21:55,381
EERIE VOICE: I'm here.

327
00:21:57,061 --> 00:21:59,101
Mother?

328
00:21:59,221 --> 00:22:01,221
EERIE VOICE: It's me.

329
00:22:03,341 --> 00:22:04,941
I'm here.

330
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:09,901
Hello.

331
00:22:12,381 --> 00:22:14,901
I'm here.

332
00:22:14,941 --> 00:22:17,381
Wait! I'm coming.

333
00:22:28,861 --> 00:22:30,701
Hello?

334
00:22:35,541 --> 00:22:37,941
EERIE VOICE: Hello.

335
00:22:39,101 --> 00:22:41,781
I'm here.

336
00:22:41,941 --> 00:22:44,101
It's me.

337
00:22:45,261 --> 00:22:46,741
Mother?

338
00:22:46,861 --> 00:22:48,301
EERIE VOICE: I'm here.

339
00:22:49,381 --> 00:22:50,941
Hello.

340
00:22:52,221 --> 00:22:54,381
Hello.

341
00:22:54,421 --> 00:22:56,581
I'm here.

342
00:23:06,061 --> 00:23:07,901
(CAWING)

343
00:23:10,301 --> 00:23:11,941
(DOGS BARKING)

344
00:23:13,421 --> 00:23:15,141
(CAWING)

345
00:23:17,141 --> 00:23:18,421
Bambi!

346
00:23:27,981 --> 00:23:29,141
Run, Bambi!

347
00:23:47,821 --> 00:23:49,541
(WHIMPERING)

348
00:23:50,341 --> 00:23:51,341
Run, Bambi!

349
00:23:52,181 --> 00:23:53,981
Go! Now!

350
00:23:56,701 --> 00:23:57,861
(GUNSHOT)

351
00:24:07,621 --> 00:24:09,861
(PANTING)

352
00:24:09,981 --> 00:24:12,541
But it was Mother.
I heard her voice.

353
00:24:12,661 --> 00:24:14,781
It was one of
man's tricks.

354
00:24:15,021 --> 00:24:16,221
I'm sorry.

355
00:24:16,301 --> 00:24:20,221
What if I hadn't
gotten there in time?
You could have been...

356
00:24:20,341 --> 00:24:23,141
When I tell you
to run, you run.

357
00:24:23,181 --> 00:24:25,741
Never freeze
like that, ever!

358
00:24:25,861 --> 00:24:29,021
I'm sorry.

359
00:24:34,061 --> 00:24:35,381
(SIGHS)

360
00:24:36,381 --> 00:24:38,701
Let's go home.

361
00:25:00,781 --> 00:25:03,221
She's never
coming back,
is she?

362
00:25:10,621 --> 00:25:12,461
No.

363
00:25:30,621 --> 00:25:32,741
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

364
00:25:50,501 --> 00:25:52,341
GREAT PRINCE:
Friend Owl.

365
00:25:52,461 --> 00:25:53,581
Hmm?

366
00:25:53,621 --> 00:25:55,981
Winter is coming
to an end.

367
00:25:56,101 --> 00:26:01,901
You should have
little trouble finding
a new home for Bambi.

368
00:26:09,341 --> 00:26:11,621
Big brother!

369
00:26:12,141 --> 00:26:15,181
Oh, big brother!

370
00:26:17,261 --> 00:26:19,461
Big brother!

371
00:26:19,501 --> 00:26:21,141
(CAWING)

372
00:26:21,981 --> 00:26:23,621
(ALL GIGGLING)

373
00:26:23,661 --> 00:26:26,941
Every time
we turn our backs,
he's gone.

374
00:26:26,981 --> 00:26:31,461
Search everywhere.
Leave no stone unturned.

375
00:26:31,501 --> 00:26:32,541
(ALL GIGGLING)

376
00:26:37,341 --> 00:26:40,181
FLOWER: How come
we're hiding from
your sisters?

377
00:26:40,221 --> 00:26:41,381
(SHUSHING)

378
00:26:41,501 --> 00:26:43,661
I think they're sweet.

379
00:26:43,821 --> 00:26:46,021
Well, you don't
have to live with them.

380
00:26:48,021 --> 00:26:49,141
(THUMPER GRUNTS)

381
00:26:49,181 --> 00:26:51,181
Back up.

382
00:26:51,221 --> 00:26:53,861
Watch it!

383
00:26:54,661 --> 00:26:56,661
Come on! Push harder!

384
00:26:57,181 --> 00:26:58,661
(FLOWER AND THUMPER
GRUNTING)

385
00:27:01,301 --> 00:27:03,701
So, where are
we off to today?

386
00:27:03,741 --> 00:27:06,581
You're going to
stay near the den,
where it's safe.

387
00:27:06,701 --> 00:27:10,701
But I'm ready for danger,
for adventure, for...

388
00:27:10,741 --> 00:27:12,541
The den.

389
00:27:12,581 --> 00:27:14,861
Yeah. Yeah, good idea.

390
00:27:14,901 --> 00:27:17,181
I'll stay and
guard the den.

391
00:27:29,541 --> 00:27:31,341
Hey, Bambi.

392
00:27:31,381 --> 00:27:32,621
What's wrong?

393
00:27:33,061 --> 00:27:34,061
Nothing.

394
00:27:34,101 --> 00:27:37,581
Come on.
You can tell
your bestest friend.

395
00:27:37,701 --> 00:27:42,741
Well, my father
never takes me
with him anymore.

396
00:27:42,861 --> 00:27:47,381
I guess I'm not
what a prince's son
is supposed to be.

397
00:27:47,541 --> 00:27:49,221
If I could
just show him.

398
00:27:49,861 --> 00:27:50,941
Show him what?

399
00:27:51,021 --> 00:27:53,781
That I can be
brave like him.

400
00:27:56,221 --> 00:28:00,461
If that's all it is,
being brave is easy.

401
00:28:00,581 --> 00:28:01,661
I can teach you.

402
00:28:01,901 --> 00:28:02,901
You can?

403
00:28:02,941 --> 00:28:05,301
Sure. Watch this.

404
00:28:06,701 --> 00:28:08,221
(GROWLING)

405
00:28:09,221 --> 00:28:11,421
(WHISPERS) I think
he's got a hairball.

406
00:28:11,461 --> 00:28:14,901
No, I'm being
brave, silly.

407
00:28:14,981 --> 00:28:19,581
The trick is to be
scarier than whatever's
scaring you. See?

408
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:21,061
(GROWLING)

409
00:28:22,461 --> 00:28:23,781
(GROWLING)

410
00:28:25,101 --> 00:28:27,101
You look like
a squirrel.

411
00:28:27,141 --> 00:28:29,221
Oh! Oh! Watch me!

412
00:28:29,421 --> 00:28:31,221
(FARTING)

413
00:28:33,101 --> 00:28:34,621
BOTH: Ew!

414
00:28:34,741 --> 00:28:35,941
Flower!

415
00:28:36,061 --> 00:28:38,821
You just found
your inner strength.

416
00:28:38,941 --> 00:28:41,821
Oh, gosh!

417
00:28:41,941 --> 00:28:44,661
Okay. Now,
stand very straight.

418
00:28:44,781 --> 00:28:46,621
Stick out your chest.

419
00:28:46,701 --> 00:28:50,941
Take the deepest breath
you ever took
in your whole life.

420
00:28:53,861 --> 00:28:57,141
Now let it out
with a big grr.

421
00:28:57,861 --> 00:28:59,061
(BLEATING)

422
00:29:00,861 --> 00:29:04,341
You're gonna need
a lot of practice.

423
00:29:04,461 --> 00:29:07,621
Come on. Do what I do.
I'm a mountain lion.

424
00:29:07,701 --> 00:29:08,741
(GROWLING)

425
00:29:08,821 --> 00:29:12,301
Oh. Oh! I'm a bear.

426
00:29:12,661 --> 00:29:13,981
(BLEATING)

427
00:29:14,541 --> 00:29:16,021
I'm a turtle.

428
00:29:16,141 --> 00:29:17,141
(GROWLING)

429
00:29:19,181 --> 00:29:23,981
What?
Turtles are so scary.

430
00:29:28,021 --> 00:29:30,181
THUMPER: Come on.
You can do it.

431
00:29:30,221 --> 00:29:31,261
(GROWLING)

432
00:29:31,341 --> 00:29:32,421
(BLEATING)

433
00:29:32,501 --> 00:29:34,261
Come on,
watch this.

434
00:29:38,021 --> 00:29:41,701
Yeah, that's it.
Come on. Try it again.

435
00:29:43,101 --> 00:29:44,341
(BLEATING)

436
00:29:44,421 --> 00:29:46,261
Yeah. That was good.

437
00:29:47,861 --> 00:29:48,861
(GROWLING)

438
00:29:48,941 --> 00:29:50,021
(BLEATING)

439
00:29:50,741 --> 00:29:51,861
(FLOWER GROWLING)

440
00:29:51,901 --> 00:29:53,541
Come on, come on!

441
00:29:54,021 --> 00:29:55,341
(BLEATING)

442
00:29:55,381 --> 00:29:56,541
(ALL SCREAMING)

443
00:30:02,741 --> 00:30:05,541
(GROWL ECHOING)

444
00:30:06,261 --> 00:30:08,701
(BLEATING ECHOING)

445
00:30:08,781 --> 00:30:10,901
Yeah, that's it.

446
00:30:11,021 --> 00:30:12,101
(GROWLING)

447
00:30:12,221 --> 00:30:13,861
(ROARING)
(BOTH GASP)

448
00:30:13,941 --> 00:30:15,701
(BOTH EXCLAIMING)

449
00:30:17,061 --> 00:30:18,701
(GIGGLING)

450
00:30:20,461 --> 00:30:21,541
(BLEATING)

451
00:30:22,541 --> 00:30:24,461
(GROWLING)

452
00:30:24,901 --> 00:30:26,301
(ALL LAUGHING)

453
00:30:28,661 --> 00:30:29,741
(GROWLING)

454
00:30:33,781 --> 00:30:34,821
(THUMPER GROWLING)

455
00:30:34,901 --> 00:30:36,141
(ALL LAUGHING)

456
00:30:39,101 --> 00:30:41,101
THUMPER: Watch this.
(GROWLING)

457
00:30:42,981 --> 00:30:44,341
(ALL LAUGHING)

458
00:30:45,581 --> 00:30:47,421
See?
There's nothing to it.

459
00:30:47,461 --> 00:30:50,741
All it takes
is one good grrr.

460
00:30:51,061 --> 00:30:52,621
(GROWLING)

461
00:30:52,741 --> 00:30:53,901
ALL: Porcupine!

462
00:30:55,421 --> 00:30:58,261
Get out and stay out,
you trespassing hooligans.

463
00:30:59,261 --> 00:31:03,181
Trashy, muddy paws.
Couldn't you
have anything nice?

464
00:31:04,581 --> 00:31:07,421
Well, we can always
swim across.

465
00:31:07,461 --> 00:31:08,661
Uh-oh.

466
00:31:11,341 --> 00:31:13,301
Let's go before
he sees you.

467
00:31:13,421 --> 00:31:14,861
No. This is it.

468
00:31:15,941 --> 00:31:18,781
I can show my dad
how brave I am.

469
00:31:19,301 --> 00:31:20,781
You better hurry.

470
00:31:26,461 --> 00:31:29,861
Don't worry.
I'll take care
of your dad.

471
00:31:33,341 --> 00:31:34,941
And remember
what I taught you.

472
00:31:35,341 --> 00:31:36,381
(GROWLING)

473
00:31:40,621 --> 00:31:41,621
(GULPS)

474
00:31:45,781 --> 00:31:48,621
I'm gonna walk
across this log.

475
00:31:48,821 --> 00:31:50,181
(BLEATING)

476
00:31:50,301 --> 00:31:53,141
Get off my property,
you pesky squirrel.

477
00:31:53,181 --> 00:31:57,061
I'm not a squirrel.
I'm the young prince.

478
00:31:57,141 --> 00:31:59,101
Where you going,
princey? (LAUGHING)

479
00:31:59,461 --> 00:32:01,461
Not this way.
Try again.

480
00:32:03,581 --> 00:32:06,821
Help! Help!
(PANTING)

481
00:32:06,901 --> 00:32:09,821
There's this thing,
and it's got these eyes,

482
00:32:09,901 --> 00:32:12,501
and these claws
like... (GROWLING)

483
00:32:12,581 --> 00:32:15,981
And it walks
around like this.
(GRUNTING)

484
00:32:16,101 --> 00:32:18,421
And, well,
you gotta see it.

485
00:32:20,661 --> 00:32:23,421
Well, come on!

486
00:32:24,421 --> 00:32:25,661
(SIGHS)

487
00:32:25,741 --> 00:32:28,341
Try again! Try again!

488
00:32:28,421 --> 00:32:31,181
You don't understand.
I have to get across.

489
00:32:31,221 --> 00:32:32,941
Go around.

490
00:32:33,021 --> 00:32:36,421
In my day,
we didn't wander willy-nilly
onto someone's property.

491
00:32:36,501 --> 00:32:38,181
We took the long way.

492
00:32:38,221 --> 00:32:42,221
It sometimes took days,
weeks, in the pouring rain,

493
00:32:42,341 --> 00:32:44,861
'cause we had
a little thing
called respect.

494
00:32:48,621 --> 00:32:50,381
Bambi, you did it!

495
00:32:50,421 --> 00:32:52,861
Yeah?
Oh, you did it
all right.

496
00:32:54,261 --> 00:32:55,381
(LAUGHING)

497
00:32:55,421 --> 00:32:56,701
FLOWER: Behind you!
Look out!

498
00:33:00,221 --> 00:33:01,541
Here I am! (LAUGHING)
(GASPING)

499
00:33:03,381 --> 00:33:04,541
Here I am again!

500
00:33:05,541 --> 00:33:07,861
Hurry up!
It's right over here.

501
00:33:08,061 --> 00:33:09,061
(PORCUPINE LAUGHING)

502
00:33:09,221 --> 00:33:11,781
(GASPS) Oops.
Wrong way.
Nothing here.

503
00:33:12,381 --> 00:33:13,621
(PORCUPINE LAUGHING)
(BAMBI GASPS)

504
00:33:13,981 --> 00:33:15,061
(EXCLAIMS)

505
00:33:17,901 --> 00:33:18,901
(GROWLING)

506
00:33:21,061 --> 00:33:22,421
(EXCLAIMS)

507
00:33:23,741 --> 00:33:25,061
(PORCUPINE LAUGHING)

508
00:33:25,381 --> 00:33:27,221
(BAMBI SQUEALING)

509
00:33:27,261 --> 00:33:28,341
What was that?

510
00:33:28,421 --> 00:33:30,581
I didn't hear anything.
Probably a bird.

511
00:33:30,621 --> 00:33:33,781
Yeah, that's it.
A bird. (GROANS)

512
00:33:33,901 --> 00:33:35,741
Oh, no.

513
00:33:35,821 --> 00:33:37,901
PORCUPINE: Ha!
That'll teach you.
(LAUGHS)

514
00:33:37,941 --> 00:33:40,941
Think twice before
you trespass
round here again.

515
00:33:41,061 --> 00:33:42,261
Mind your own
beeswax next time.

516
00:33:42,341 --> 00:33:43,341
(GASPS)

517
00:33:46,661 --> 00:33:48,581
(GROWLING)

518
00:33:50,581 --> 00:33:52,741
That's the problem
with these kids today.

519
00:33:52,901 --> 00:33:55,061
No respect.
No respect at all.

520
00:33:55,101 --> 00:33:58,061
What are you looking at,
you big moose?

521
00:33:59,941 --> 00:34:00,941
(CLEARING THROAT)

522
00:34:01,941 --> 00:34:03,301
(LAUGHING NERVOUSLY)

523
00:34:05,141 --> 00:34:06,221
(SIGHS)

524
00:34:13,981 --> 00:34:15,781
(PANTING)

525
00:34:19,581 --> 00:34:22,581
(GASPS) Bambi,
are you okay?

526
00:34:22,941 --> 00:34:24,981
(GROANS)
How does it look?

527
00:34:26,781 --> 00:34:28,341
BOTH: Ew!

528
00:34:28,461 --> 00:34:32,421
I'm not
gonna lie to you.
It ain't pretty.

529
00:34:32,461 --> 00:34:34,981
It's hopeless.
I'm a coward.

530
00:34:35,021 --> 00:34:37,581
No. You're brave.
Ow!

531
00:34:37,621 --> 00:34:41,101
No one's ever
got that far
across before.

532
00:34:41,141 --> 00:34:42,181
Ow!

533
00:34:42,701 --> 00:34:46,101
That's the great
thing about me.
I don't feel any pain.

534
00:34:46,821 --> 00:34:49,301
(SCOFFS) Watch this.

535
00:34:49,621 --> 00:34:50,821
(YELLING)

536
00:34:52,461 --> 00:34:54,941
See? Nothing.

537
00:34:55,341 --> 00:34:56,621
(BAMBI EXCLAIMING IN PAIN)

538
00:34:56,661 --> 00:34:57,701
What was that?

539
00:34:57,821 --> 00:34:59,821
Probably just some poor,
dumb animal

540
00:34:59,981 --> 00:35:02,021
caught in a trap.
So anyways...

541
00:35:02,381 --> 00:35:03,621
(BAMBI EXCLAIMING IN PAIN)

542
00:35:03,661 --> 00:35:04,861
(GASPS) Bambi!

543
00:35:05,181 --> 00:35:08,461
Hey! I wasn't finished
talking about me.

544
00:35:09,501 --> 00:35:10,741
Just one more.

545
00:35:10,821 --> 00:35:13,181
Bambi, what happened?

546
00:35:13,221 --> 00:35:15,621
Bambi got stuck
by a porcupine.

547
00:35:15,661 --> 00:35:18,461
A porcupine? Where?
THUMPER: Hold still!

548
00:35:18,501 --> 00:35:20,181
It was nothing.
Are you hurt?

549
00:35:20,301 --> 00:35:21,301
THUMPER: Stop moving!

550
00:35:21,341 --> 00:35:23,501
I'm fine. Really.
It's just...

551
00:35:23,541 --> 00:35:24,701
Ow!

552
00:35:25,381 --> 00:35:26,821
Got it.

553
00:35:26,861 --> 00:35:30,701
Bambi. I thought
I recognized that scream.

554
00:35:30,741 --> 00:35:32,541
I'm surprised to
see you moving.

555
00:35:32,661 --> 00:35:34,341
It was only
a porcupine.

556
00:35:34,501 --> 00:35:36,181
No, no, no.

557
00:35:36,261 --> 00:35:39,221
I'm talking about
how you froze
out on the meadow,

558
00:35:39,381 --> 00:35:42,221
and right in front
of your father.

559
00:35:42,261 --> 00:35:43,661
FALINE: Ronno!

560
00:35:43,781 --> 00:35:45,221
RONNO: Don't feel bad.

561
00:35:45,261 --> 00:35:50,061
If we didn't have cowards,
we couldn't tell
who the brave ones are.

562
00:35:50,501 --> 00:35:52,021
I'm not a coward.

563
00:35:52,501 --> 00:35:53,581
(BLEATING)

564
00:35:54,421 --> 00:35:58,741
Oh. Yeah, sure.
Come on. Let's go.

565
00:35:58,741 --> 00:36:01,541
I'm staying here.
Come on.

566
00:36:01,701 --> 00:36:03,381
Ronno, quit it.

567
00:36:03,461 --> 00:36:05,461
Leave her alone.

568
00:36:05,901 --> 00:36:09,741
Did you say
something, Bambi?

569
00:36:09,861 --> 00:36:11,541
No. Well...

570
00:36:11,581 --> 00:36:13,741
I mean, yes.

571
00:36:14,781 --> 00:36:18,061
Leave her alone.
Please?

572
00:36:18,181 --> 00:36:19,781
You tell him, Bambi.

573
00:36:19,901 --> 00:36:24,781
Oh, wook.
It's the wittle bunny
and the wittle skunk.

574
00:36:24,901 --> 00:36:29,101
Does the young prince
play with the wittle bunny
and the wittle skunk?

575
00:36:30,741 --> 00:36:31,781
(GROANS)

576
00:36:31,941 --> 00:36:33,061
(GASPS)

577
00:36:33,101 --> 00:36:34,141
(GROWLING)

578
00:36:34,261 --> 00:36:35,381
THUMPER: Run!

579
00:36:36,701 --> 00:36:37,741
(GASPS)

580
00:36:39,101 --> 00:36:41,421
FALINE: Run, Bambi!

581
00:36:42,221 --> 00:36:43,261
(THUMPER EXCLAIMS)

582
00:36:43,741 --> 00:36:44,941
(SCREECHING)

583
00:36:51,941 --> 00:36:52,981
(GROWLING)

584
00:36:56,621 --> 00:36:57,901
(EXCLAIMING)
(GASPS)

585
00:36:58,261 --> 00:37:00,461
Other way! Other way!

586
00:37:01,501 --> 00:37:04,101
Turn around!
Turn around!

587
00:37:08,461 --> 00:37:10,461
(BOTH SCREAMING)

588
00:37:14,621 --> 00:37:17,621
(GASPS) We made it.

589
00:37:20,421 --> 00:37:22,261
THUMPER:
What's the matter?

590
00:37:22,301 --> 00:37:23,781
Too scared?

591
00:37:23,861 --> 00:37:27,981
(LAUGHING) Look at him.
Look at him shaking.

592
00:37:28,021 --> 00:37:31,661
Now who's the baby,
you big baby?

593
00:37:31,701 --> 00:37:32,981
(GASPS)
Whoa!

594
00:37:34,621 --> 00:37:36,501
(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY) Hello.

595
00:37:36,541 --> 00:37:38,341
I told you to
stay near the den.

596
00:37:38,461 --> 00:37:42,501
When I give you an order,
I expect you to...

597
00:37:43,701 --> 00:37:45,341
How did you...

598
00:37:46,821 --> 00:37:48,821
Did you jump?

599
00:37:49,821 --> 00:37:51,301
Yes, sir.

600
00:37:51,821 --> 00:37:55,381
Hmm. I didn't make
a jump like that
until I had antlers.

601
00:38:06,021 --> 00:38:08,221
Yes.
(CLEARING THROAT) Well...

602
00:38:09,301 --> 00:38:12,181
We should be going

603
00:38:13,901 --> 00:38:15,181
home.

604
00:38:16,061 --> 00:38:19,221
He's never said
anything nice
like that before.

605
00:38:19,381 --> 00:38:21,421
I guess he saw
how brave you were.

606
00:38:22,061 --> 00:38:25,901
Gosh, what a jump.
It was like flying.

607
00:38:26,021 --> 00:38:30,221
What's the big deal?
Anyone can make that jump.

608
00:38:30,861 --> 00:38:32,301
(GRUNTING)

609
00:38:33,901 --> 00:38:35,301
(SCREAMING)

610
00:38:48,381 --> 00:38:51,901
Come on.
You jumped further
than this yesterday.

611
00:38:51,981 --> 00:38:54,741
I don't know.

612
00:38:54,781 --> 00:38:57,461
You're not afraid,
are you?

613
00:38:58,621 --> 00:39:01,901
(MOCKINGLY)
You're too afraid.
You cannot jump...

614
00:39:02,101 --> 00:39:05,141
(EXCLAIMING MOCKINGLY)

615
00:39:06,781 --> 00:39:07,941
(SCREAMING)

616
00:39:10,741 --> 00:39:12,461
You did it.
Whoo-hoo!

617
00:39:12,541 --> 00:39:13,541
Let's do it again.

618
00:39:13,581 --> 00:39:15,461
And this time
put it out further.

619
00:39:15,941 --> 00:39:17,941
Come on, Bambi.
You can do it.

620
00:39:18,421 --> 00:39:20,501
Wait till your dad
sees this.

621
00:39:20,581 --> 00:39:21,781
(FRIEND OWL CHUCKLING)

622
00:39:21,941 --> 00:39:23,501
Good morning, sir.

623
00:39:23,621 --> 00:39:25,261
(CLEARING THROAT)
Morning, Owl.

624
00:39:25,301 --> 00:39:30,021
Just thought I'd let you know
that the search is off
to a flying start.

625
00:39:30,301 --> 00:39:31,861
Oh! Yes, well,

626
00:39:31,941 --> 00:39:34,141
no pun intended,

627
00:39:34,261 --> 00:39:38,341
with the flying,
as I'm an owl.

628
00:39:39,101 --> 00:39:41,821
(CLEARING THROAT)
Yes, well.

629
00:39:41,941 --> 00:39:44,341
I've met with
several does already

630
00:39:44,461 --> 00:39:45,941
who would make
excellent mothers.

631
00:39:46,021 --> 00:39:48,661
BAMBI:
Put it out further!

632
00:39:48,781 --> 00:39:51,461
Unless you've
changed your mind?

633
00:39:51,541 --> 00:39:54,221
No, I have not.

634
00:39:54,301 --> 00:39:55,541
(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)

635
00:39:55,621 --> 00:39:58,541
Hey, watch this!
Watch this!

636
00:39:58,621 --> 00:39:59,701
(EXCLAIMS)

637
00:39:59,781 --> 00:40:00,981
Did I make it?

638
00:40:01,021 --> 00:40:02,981
Yep. You did it.

639
00:40:05,141 --> 00:40:06,981
What exactly
are you doing?

640
00:40:07,101 --> 00:40:08,981
I'm practicing my jumps.

641
00:40:09,021 --> 00:40:10,901
Yeah. See?

642
00:40:11,221 --> 00:40:13,621
Mmm. I see.

643
00:40:17,981 --> 00:40:21,861
I don't get it.
Yesterday he really
liked it.

644
00:40:21,981 --> 00:40:24,741
What's he doing,
anyway?

645
00:40:24,821 --> 00:40:28,541
(SIGHS) I don't know,
but he sure does
an awful lot of it.

646
00:40:28,661 --> 00:40:30,421
Well, why don't
you ask him?

647
00:40:30,501 --> 00:40:33,541
Oh, he looks busy.
I better not.

648
00:40:33,661 --> 00:40:36,421
Parents like it
when you ask them
questions,

649
00:40:36,501 --> 00:40:39,341
lots and lots
of questions.

650
00:40:39,421 --> 00:40:40,781
Really?

651
00:40:40,821 --> 00:40:42,981
Go on.
I'm right behind you.

652
00:40:46,741 --> 00:40:47,861
(LAUGHS)

653
00:40:54,181 --> 00:40:55,421
(GASPING)

654
00:40:55,861 --> 00:40:56,941
(GIGGLING)

655
00:40:58,221 --> 00:40:59,701
Um... Uh...

656
00:41:00,421 --> 00:41:02,021
(LAUGHING NERVOUSLY)

657
00:41:02,101 --> 00:41:03,621
What are you doing?

658
00:41:03,741 --> 00:41:05,261
Observing.

659
00:41:05,541 --> 00:41:08,021
Oh. Observing.

660
00:41:09,901 --> 00:41:11,581
What's observing?

661
00:41:11,701 --> 00:41:13,421
Well, it's...

662
00:41:14,461 --> 00:41:16,301
It's...

663
00:41:16,381 --> 00:41:17,541
(SIGHS)

664
00:41:17,621 --> 00:41:19,421
It's difficult
to explain.

665
00:41:19,901 --> 00:41:21,221
Oh.

666
00:41:24,261 --> 00:41:27,101
You have to look, listen,

667
00:41:27,701 --> 00:41:30,421
and smell,
all at the same time.

668
00:41:30,541 --> 00:41:32,541
Oh, I can do that.

669
00:41:32,581 --> 00:41:34,581
Look, listen, smell.

670
00:41:34,741 --> 00:41:36,541
(SNIFFING)

671
00:41:37,621 --> 00:41:39,261
Hmm.

672
00:41:39,381 --> 00:41:42,141
Try to feel
the forest around you.

673
00:41:47,461 --> 00:41:49,421
I don't feel anything.

674
00:41:50,461 --> 00:41:52,181
Does playing
in the meadow.

675
00:41:52,701 --> 00:41:54,061
How do you know?

676
00:41:54,101 --> 00:41:56,581
I feel it
in my hooves.

677
00:41:56,661 --> 00:42:01,261
If there was danger,
they'd know to stomp,
and I'd run to them.

678
00:42:01,301 --> 00:42:02,981
But wouldn't you
be scared?

679
00:42:03,101 --> 00:42:05,821
Perhaps,
but I would still
run to them.

680
00:42:05,941 --> 00:42:11,861
A prince may be afraid,
but he can't let fear
stop him from acting.

681
00:42:11,941 --> 00:42:15,021
Wow. You know everything.

682
00:42:15,101 --> 00:42:16,581
(LAUGHING)

683
00:42:16,661 --> 00:42:18,261
Not everything.

684
00:42:19,821 --> 00:42:22,821
Well, the forest
is waiting.

685
00:42:28,941 --> 00:42:30,141
Are you coming?

686
00:42:31,661 --> 00:42:33,781
Oh! Sure!

687
00:42:40,301 --> 00:42:42,021
RABBIT 1: Big brother!
RABBIT 2: Big brother!

688
00:42:42,141 --> 00:42:44,861
Oh, for crying out loud!

689
00:42:44,981 --> 00:42:47,861
Feel the forest.
Feel the forest.

690
00:42:47,941 --> 00:42:49,861
Feel the forest.
Bambi!

691
00:42:49,981 --> 00:42:52,541
Feel the...
(LAUGHS SHEEPISHLY)

692
00:42:52,621 --> 00:42:54,461
Felt it.

693
00:43:01,461 --> 00:43:05,581
WOMAN:
♪ Why does winter
always make you wait

694
00:43:05,661 --> 00:43:09,381
♪ For a glimpse of sun?

695
00:43:09,501 --> 00:43:13,501
♪ Takes a simple
clue or leap of faith

696
00:43:13,541 --> 00:43:16,381
♪ To know the time will come

697
00:43:16,501 --> 00:43:19,581
♪ When long, cold nights

698
00:43:19,661 --> 00:43:24,221
♪ Fade into memory
looking at the morning light

699
00:43:24,341 --> 00:43:29,941
♪ And we will be together

700
00:43:30,021 --> 00:43:33,581
♪ Leaving our cares
behind forever

701
00:43:33,661 --> 00:43:36,741
♪ At the first
sign of spring

702
00:43:36,861 --> 00:43:41,701
♪ The heat of the sun
will shine right through

703
00:43:41,781 --> 00:43:45,621
♪ And never a moment
comes too soon

704
00:43:45,701 --> 00:43:49,341
♪ As the first
sign of spring

705
00:43:50,581 --> 00:43:51,861
(GROWLING)
(GASPS)

706
00:43:56,181 --> 00:43:57,461
Whoa!
(ALL GIGGLING)

707
00:43:57,541 --> 00:44:01,701
♪ Air is getting
warmer by the day

708
00:44:01,781 --> 00:44:04,701
♪ As the thaw begins

709
00:44:05,701 --> 00:44:09,421
♪ So put a corner
on this page

710
00:44:09,541 --> 00:44:12,541
♪ The leaves are green again

711
00:44:12,581 --> 00:44:14,381
♪ And cloudy skies

712
00:44:14,461 --> 00:44:16,301
I hear it, I hear it!

713
00:44:16,381 --> 00:44:20,381
♪ Are lifting away
right in front
of our very eyes

714
00:44:20,461 --> 00:44:26,421
♪ And we will be together

715
00:44:29,981 --> 00:44:32,901
♪ At the first
sign of spring

716
00:44:32,941 --> 00:44:34,221
(SCOFFS)

717
00:44:39,901 --> 00:44:41,901
When will I get
my antlers?

718
00:44:41,941 --> 00:44:43,141
(CHUCKLES)

719
00:44:43,261 --> 00:44:46,741
Won't be long now
if you're anything
like I was.

720
00:44:47,261 --> 00:44:48,501
Am I?

721
00:44:48,581 --> 00:44:51,741
Well, only one way
to find out.

722
00:44:57,621 --> 00:44:59,501
Wow!

723
00:44:59,581 --> 00:45:02,661
♪ At the first
sign of spring

724
00:45:04,661 --> 00:45:08,421
♪ A new season's begun

725
00:45:08,461 --> 00:45:12,141
♪ For a father and son

726
00:45:12,261 --> 00:45:16,181
♪ And everything grows
a little faster

727
00:45:16,261 --> 00:45:20,381
♪ And every moment
stretches longer

728
00:45:20,461 --> 00:45:25,461
♪ And it will only
get much stronger

729
00:45:27,621 --> 00:45:32,461
♪ We will be together

730
00:45:32,541 --> 00:45:35,701
♪ Leaving our cares
behind forever

731
00:45:35,781 --> 00:45:37,141
Whoo-hoo!

732
00:45:37,221 --> 00:45:39,221
♪ At the first
sign of spring

733
00:45:39,301 --> 00:45:43,981
♪ The heat of the sun
will shine right through

734
00:45:44,461 --> 00:45:48,821
♪ Never a moment
comes too soon

735
00:45:48,861 --> 00:45:52,381
♪ As the first
sign of spring

736
00:45:52,501 --> 00:45:55,501
♪ At the first
sign of spring

737
00:45:56,501 --> 00:46:02,541
♪ At the first
sign of spring ♪

738
00:46:20,341 --> 00:46:22,421
(BAMBI GIGGLING)

739
00:46:22,501 --> 00:46:25,341
GREAT PRINCE: Bambi,
time to go to sleep.

740
00:46:26,061 --> 00:46:29,021
But I can't sleep.
I'm wide awake.

741
00:46:29,061 --> 00:46:30,781
Try.

742
00:46:30,861 --> 00:46:33,101
Okay, I'll try.

743
00:46:34,941 --> 00:46:36,741
(BAMBI GIGGLING)

744
00:46:36,861 --> 00:46:39,021
It was funny
when you chased
that cricket,

745
00:46:39,101 --> 00:46:41,301
then there
was one more,
then one more.

746
00:46:41,381 --> 00:46:43,621
Yes, yes.

747
00:46:43,701 --> 00:46:46,061
Now, get some sleep.

748
00:46:47,861 --> 00:46:49,541
Flower sleeps
all winter.

749
00:46:49,581 --> 00:46:50,861
(SIGHS)

750
00:46:50,901 --> 00:46:52,221
Why do we sleep?

751
00:46:52,541 --> 00:46:55,141
Everything must get rest.

752
00:46:55,221 --> 00:46:58,901
Some at night,
some during the day.

753
00:47:00,141 --> 00:47:02,541
Some not at all.

754
00:47:04,621 --> 00:47:05,901
(GREAT PRINCE CHUCKLING)

755
00:47:08,221 --> 00:47:10,461
Mother's resting now,
isn't she?

756
00:47:10,541 --> 00:47:12,221
Oh, I forgot.

757
00:47:12,301 --> 00:47:16,821
A prince leaves the past
in the past, right?

758
00:47:20,581 --> 00:47:22,941
That's enough
questions for today.

759
00:47:23,061 --> 00:47:24,821
Now, please
get some sleep.

760
00:47:24,901 --> 00:47:26,901
Okay.

761
00:47:27,901 --> 00:47:29,661
Good night.

762
00:47:33,581 --> 00:47:34,901
(SIGHING)

763
00:48:08,981 --> 00:48:10,341
(GROWLING)

764
00:48:12,781 --> 00:48:14,381
(GREAT PRINCE YAWNING)

765
00:48:14,461 --> 00:48:17,141
BAMBI: Come on,
sleepyhead. (LAUGHING)

766
00:48:17,221 --> 00:48:21,701
Remind me
never to let you eat
blossoms before bedtime.

767
00:48:21,781 --> 00:48:23,861
Wait. I hear trouble.

768
00:48:23,981 --> 00:48:25,541
What? What?
(GASPS)

769
00:48:25,621 --> 00:48:28,021
Hornet nest,
antler-high.

770
00:48:29,141 --> 00:48:31,381
Very good.

771
00:48:31,461 --> 00:48:32,821
Wait!
(GASPS)

772
00:48:32,861 --> 00:48:35,301
Now I see trouble.
Where? Where?

773
00:48:35,341 --> 00:48:37,661
Rival stag, dead ahead.

774
00:48:37,701 --> 00:48:40,821
He's pretty small.
Shouldn't be any trouble.

775
00:48:40,861 --> 00:48:43,901
Oh, yeah?
I can be plenty
of trouble.

776
00:48:43,981 --> 00:48:45,621
No, not you.

777
00:48:45,741 --> 00:48:47,301
Yes, me.

778
00:48:48,541 --> 00:48:50,821
Now you've had it.

779
00:48:52,181 --> 00:48:53,341
Gotcha!

780
00:48:53,381 --> 00:48:55,581
Now who's got who?

781
00:48:55,661 --> 00:48:57,221
(BLOWING RASPBERRY)

782
00:48:57,341 --> 00:48:58,861
FRIEND OWL:
There you two are.
Well, yes.

783
00:48:59,501 --> 00:49:00,621
Hello, Friend Owl.

784
00:49:00,661 --> 00:49:02,661
Well, hello.

785
00:49:02,701 --> 00:49:05,861
(CLEARING THROAT)
I've been meaning
to speak to you.

786
00:49:05,861 --> 00:49:07,741
I've been
looking everywhere.

787
00:49:07,861 --> 00:49:09,581
I thought you'd be
by the meadow now.

788
00:49:09,661 --> 00:49:12,181
I'm afraid I got
a little (GRUNTS)

789
00:49:12,221 --> 00:49:13,421
